rgin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135708157.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A motorist rescued a severely dehydrated sambar deer found beside Singapore's Bukit Timah Expressway on November 8. NParks took it to the Mandai Wildlife Centre, where veterinarians provided treatment and monitored it overnight. After its condition improved, the fawn was released near the spot where it was found on November 9.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/a-motorist-spotted-a-severely-dehydrated-young-deer-beside-a-singapore-expressway-and-called-rescuers-after-emergency-veterinary-treatment-and-overnight-monitoring-it-was-released-near-where-it-was-found/articleshow/135708157.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/a-motorist-spotted-a-severely-dehydrated-young-deer-beside-a-singapore-expressway-and-called-rescuers-after-emergency-veterinary-treatment-and-overnight-monitoring-it-was-released-near-where-it-was-found/articleshow/135708157.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T20:07:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135708709,imgsize-70066.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California teen turns free science workshops into a global 21-chapter nonprofit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135708466.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-teen-katelyn-liu-launches-nonprofit-to-inspire-thousands-with-free-stem-workshops-and-kits/articleshow/135708466.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-teen-katelyn-liu-launches-nonprofit-to-inspire-thousands-with-free-stem-workshops-and-kits/articleshow/135708466.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T20:04:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135708703,imgsize-754436.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[8,000 frog bones in Roman ditch traced to ancient birds of prey feast]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135711108.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-found-8000-frog-bones-in-one-roman-era-ditch-in-england-and-spent-a-decade-trying-to-explain-them-a-new-study-suggests-birds-of-prey-feasted-on-young-frogs-around-1700-years-ago/articleshow/135711108.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-found-8000-frog-bones-in-one-roman-era-ditch-in-england-and-spent-a-decade-trying-to-explain-them-a-new-study-suggests-birds-of-prey-feasted-on-young-frogs-around-1700-years-ago/articleshow/135711108.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135711186,imgsize-674761.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Washington court upholds home ownership ruling in $132,000 loan dispute between family friends]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135711238.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A mortgage deal between Lorrie D. Carlson and Sonny H. Hwang spiraled into a series of legal battles. After Carlson lent Hwang $132,000, secured by a shared property, tensions arose when Hwang neglected his payments. Proceedings ensued as Hwang filed claims against Carlson. The appeals court deemed no consumer law breaches by Carlson but confirmed Hwang's clear title ownership, sending the case back for discussions on Carlson's attorney fee recovery.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-woman-paid-for-a-family-friends-first-home-in-2018-and-took-shared-title-to-secure-a-132000-loan-after-he-stopped-paying-a-court-upheld-his-ownership-while-rejecting-his-claims-against-her/articleshow/135711238.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-woman-paid-for-a-family-friends-first-home-in-2018-and-took-shared-title-to-secure-a-132000-loan-after-he-stopped-paying-a-court-upheld-his-ownership-while-rejecting-his-claims-against-her/articleshow/135711238.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T19:36:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135713026,imgsize-73955.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indiana couple withhold home payment over construction defects, lose appeal against builder]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135703047.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Indiana couple withheld the remaining payment for a $211,235 modular home, citing construction problems. The Indiana Court of Appeals upheld a $221,704 judgment against them, finding that the builder had substantially performed its contractual obligations and that the couple had prevented it from completing the remaining work.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-couple-paid-100000-toward-a-211235-modular-home-but-withheld-the-balance-after-citing-construction-problems-a-november-9-appeals-court-upheld-a-judgment-exceeding-221000-against-them/articleshow/135703047.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-couple-paid-100000-toward-a-211235-modular-home-but-withheld-the-balance-after-citing-construction-problems-a-november-9-appeals-court-upheld-a-judgment-exceeding-221000-against-them/articleshow/135703047.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T19:34:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135703689,imgsize-234862.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[F.P. Journe Watch Sells for $10.59 Million in Geneva]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135712182.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The recent Phillips auction in Geneva set a new benchmark in the luxury watch market, generating an impressive CHF 92 million in total sales. Each timepiece captivated enthusiasts, with every watch successfully sold. A standout piece, the F.P. Journe Chronomètre à Résonance 'Régence', commanded a staggering CHF 8.68 million, alongside notable sales like a Patek Philippe for CHF 6,267,000 and a Cartier watch for CHF 4,815,000.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rare-platinum-f-p-journe-wristwatch-with-a-hand-engraved-pink-gold-dial-sold-for-10-59-million-in-geneva-the-two-day-auction-made-history-by-selling-all-217-watches-for-a-combined-112-3-million/articleshow/135712182.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rare-platinum-f-p-journe-wristwatch-with-a-hand-engraved-pink-gold-dial-sold-for-10-59-million-in-geneva-the-two-day-auction-made-history-by-selling-all-217-watches-for-a-combined-112-3-million/articleshow/135712182.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T19:30:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135712294,imgsize-62334.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Germany funds Pacific restoration: €20m backs seven-year island project]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135709882.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Germany is allocating €20 million to restore biodiversity on islands in Palau, Samoa, Tonga, and Wallis and Futuna. The funding will support the ‘Restoring Pacific Islands for Nature and People’ project over the next seven years. Local communities, national governments, and partnerships will play a critical role in this initiative. Key efforts will focus on removing invasive species and reviving native ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/germany-backs-20-million-project-to-restore-native-wildlife-protect-pacific-island-ecosystems-and-strengthen-climate-resilience-across-palau-samoa-tonga-and-wallis-and-futuna/articleshow/135709882.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/germany-backs-20-million-project-to-restore-native-wildlife-protect-pacific-island-ecosystems-and-strengthen-climate-resilience-across-palau-samoa-tonga-and-wallis-and-futuna/articleshow/135709882.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T19:30:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135710447,imgsize-229898.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ex-teacher jailed for threatening to shoot Tory leader Kemi Badenoch in racist emails]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135712237.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ex-teacher-jailed-for-threatening-to-shoot-tory-leader-kemi-badenoch-in-racist-emails/articleshow/135712237.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ex-teacher-jailed-for-threatening-to-shoot-tory-leader-kemi-badenoch-in-racist-emails/articleshow/135712237.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T19:06:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135712405,imgsize-1014392.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ICE arrests Iranian 'King of Instagram' Farzad Tony who was living in the US illegally, flaunting luxury cars, partying with naked models]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135712113.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-arrests-iranian-king-of-instagram-farzad-tony-who-was-living-in-the-us-illegally-flaunting-luxury-cars-partying-with-naked-models/articleshow/135712113.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-arrests-iranian-king-of-instagram-farzad-tony-who-was-living-in-the-us-illegally-flaunting-luxury-cars-partying-with-naked-models/articleshow/135712113.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T18:56:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135712190,imgsize-26720.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kentucky appeals court finds no threat, overturns woman's stalking protection order]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135675859.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Kentucky, Abigail Taylor Harbin alleged that Billie West engaged in stalking behavior stemming from incidents at Chuck E. Cheese, linked to family disputes during her aunt's divorce from David Hensley. Despite her claims of repeated harassment, the Court of Appeals found insufficient evidence of actual threats and ruled that the family court had overstepped by granting the protection order, ultimately dismissing Harbin's petition against West.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-woman-obtained-a-stalking-protection-order-after-repeated-encounters-with-a-woman-linked-to-her-aunts-divorce-at-chuck-e-cheese-an-appeals-court-overturned-it-finding-no-evidence-of-a-threat/articleshow/135675859.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-woman-obtained-a-stalking-protection-order-after-repeated-encounters-with-a-woman-linked-to-her-aunts-divorce-at-chuck-e-cheese-an-appeals-court-overturned-it-finding-no-evidence-of-a-threat/articleshow/135675859.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T18:42:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135675894,imgsize-2093843.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[State Challenges Tribal Land Status: New York State sues US agencies; Seneca Nation vows to defend sovereignty]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135702045.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New York State has initiated a legal confrontation with the federal government over land ownership issues involving the Seneca Nation. This case centers on a 207-acre parcel on Grand Island, which the Seneca Nation claims as part of their ancestral territory. Having been granted restricted-fee status, the Nation has more control over the land's utilization.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-has-sued-the-federal-government-over-a-207-acre-island-property-donated-to-the-seneca-nation-for-1-seeking-to-undo-federal-approval-of-its-protected-land-status-as-the-tribe-vows-to-defend-its-rights/articleshow/135702045.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-has-sued-the-federal-government-over-a-207-acre-island-property-donated-to-the-seneca-nation-for-1-seeking-to-undo-federal-approval-of-its-protected-land-status-as-the-tribe-vows-to-defend-its-rights/articleshow/135702045.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T18:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135702078,imgsize-875602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Steve Wynn’s $70 million Central Park penthouse goes under contract after years on market]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135711394.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After four long years on the market, Steve Wynn has finally sold his impressive 10,875-square-foot Central Park penthouse for $70 million. The property, initially met with hesitation from buyers due to its limited number of bedrooms, is celebrated for its stunning views of the park and its luxurious, hotel-like amenities. This sale marks a significant moment in the evolving landscape of Manhattan's luxury real estate market.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2012-casino-billionaire-steve-wynn-paid-70-million-for-a-central-park-penthouse-after-asking-90-million-in-2022-and-cutting-the-price-the-10875-square-foot-duplex-finally-went-under-contract-in-november-2026/articleshow/135711394.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2012-casino-billionaire-steve-wynn-paid-70-million-for-a-central-park-penthouse-after-asking-90-million-in-2022-and-cutting-the-price-the-10875-square-foot-duplex-finally-went-under-contract-in-november-2026/articleshow/135711394.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T18:37:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">